Upgrade procedure for wpa_supplicant and hostapd (contrib/wpa)

Sources:
  https://w1.fi/releases/wpa_supplicant-VERSION.tar.gz
  https://w1.fi/releases/hostapd-VERSION.tar.gz
  (plus the matching .tar.gz.asc signatures)

Both tarballs are signed by Jouni Malinen <j@w1.fi>, key fingerprint
EC4A A0A9 91A5 F246 4582  D52D 2B6E F432 EFC8 95FA.  Verify both
signatures before importing.

Vendor branch:	vendor/wpa/dist (not pruned, no Xlist)
Tag:		vendor/wpa/dist/VERSION
In-tree prefix:	contrib/wpa
Build glue:	usr.sbin/wpa

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Download and verify both tarballs into an empty directory.
2. Extract the wpa_supplicant tarball, then extract the hostapd tarball
   over it (tar -C <dir> --strip-components=1).  The files the two
   tarballs share (COPYING, README, src/ and so on) were identical in
   2.11 and 2.12; check this with cmp before overlaying and note any
   difference in the vendor commit message.
3. Use the vendor-update skill (vendor/wpa/dist, contrib/wpa).  Stage
   the import with "git add -A -f": upstream ships .gitignore files
   that otherwise drop the docbook manual pages, vs2005 project
   directories, binder/fi and hostapd/logwatch/hostapd.  Commit it as
   "Vendor import of wpa + hostapd VERSION" on top of the previous
   vendor commit and tag it.
4. Merge it into contrib/wpa with "git subtree merge -P contrib/wpa"
   (a real merge commit, never a squash) and resolve conflicts by
   keeping the local patches below.
5. Update the SRCS lists and CFLAGS in usr.sbin/wpa for added and
   removed upstream sources.  FreeBSD's usr.sbin/wpa is the closest
   reference.
6. Build usr.sbin/wpa and run "wpa_supplicant -v" and "hostapd -v".

Local changes carried in contrib/wpa on top of upstream:

  - src/radius/radius.c (upstream aa02cfa569477f67f3915c8b9a83d1a7ca93693d,
    w1.fi 2026-5): radius_msg_verify_das_req() and
    radius_msg_verify_msg_auth() reject a Message-Authenticator
    attribute whose length is not sizeof(*attr) + MD5_MAC_LEN.  Drop
    this when importing hostapd 2.12.1 or later.
  - src/drivers/driver_bsd.c (FreeBSD): net80211 changes.
    * bsd_get_iface_flags() is replaced by bsd_ctrl_iface(priv, enable),
      which also sets or clears IFF_UP; it is called from
      bsd_set_ieee8021x(), bsd_init() and wpa_driver_bsd_init() (mark
      down during setup), bsd_deinit() and wpa_driver_bsd_deinit()
      (mark down), and wpa_driver_bsd_associate() and
      wpa_driver_bsd_scan() (mark up).
    * RTM_IFINFO handling in bsd_wireless_event_receive() also looks
      at IFF_RUNNING.
    * wpa_driver_bsd_set_rsn_wpa_ie() is added; associate() looks up
      the RSN IE, else the WPA vendor IE, and programs it with that.
    * IBSS uses IFM_IEEE80211_ADHOC; get80211opmode() reports
      IEEE80211_M_IBSS.
    * wpa_driver_bsd_capa() always advertises WEP40/WEP104/TKIP/CCMP
      under __MidnightBSD__ because net80211 does software crypto.
    * bsd_global_init() opens the ioctl socket with PF_LOCAL (FreeBSD
      6aeec6a74197) instead of upstream's PF_INET with a PF_INET6
      fallback.
    * (MidnightBSD) All four __FreeBSD__ tests in the file, three of
      them upstream's, use __MidnightBSD__ instead.  Our compilers
      define both, so this changes no code.
  - src/l2_packet/l2_packet_freebsd.c (FreeBSD): include <net/bpf.h>
    when __FreeBSD_version is defined, and use pcap_next_ex() so a
    vanished device terminates the event loop.
  - src/ap/hostapd.c (FreeBSD): in setup_interface2(), an
    "#ifdef __FreeBSD" block (no trailing underscores, so currently
    never compiled) that skips hostapd_get_hw_features().
  - src/common/dhcp.h (FreeBSD): map Linux struct iphdr field names to
    struct ip under __FreeBSD__.
  - src/utils/os_unix.c (FreeBSD): os_fdatasync() is not built on
    __DragonFly__.
  - src/wps/wps_upnp.c (FreeBSD): get_netif_info() uses eth_get() on
    __DragonFly__ as well.
  - src/drivers/driver_ndis.c (FreeBSD): printf format fixes and
    dup_binstr() replaced by os_malloc()/os_memcpy() in
    wpa_driver_ndis_get_names().  Not built.
  - wpa_supplicant/ctrl_iface_unix.c (FreeBSD): in
    wpas_ctrl_iface_open_sock(), raise SO_SNDBUF to CTRL_IFACE_MAX_LEN
    under __FreeBSD__.
  - wpa_supplicant/main.c (FreeBSD): usage() lists "bsd,wired"
    drivers and uses "-Dbsd" in the example.
  - wpa_supplicant/wpa_cli.c (FreeBSD): wpa_cli_action_process() runs
    the action script for WPA_EVENT_TEMP_DISABLED.
  - wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.c (FreeBSD): the
    CONFIG_DRIVER_NDIS driver_ndis_init_ops() call is removed from
    wpa_supplicant_init().
  - Files kept from older releases, not built: src/ap/iapp.[ch],
    wpa_supplicant/blacklist.[ch].
  - Files removed locally: wpa_supplicant/wpa_gui-qt4/,
    wpa_supplicant/win_if_list.c, wpa_supplicant/win_example.reg and
    src/eap_peer/.gitignore.
  - wpa_supplicant/vs2005/{wpa_supplicant.sln,win_if_list/*.vcproj,
    wpasvc/*.vcproj} have LF instead of CRLF line endings.

Local patches dropped at 2.12:

  - src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c: link ID bounds check in
    hostapd_process_ml_assoc_req() (ec3614ffcc).  Fixed upstream in
